# ============================================================================
# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules (also honoured by Netlify).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: `output: 'export'` produces a folder of static files and
# no server, so Next's `redirects()` config is unavailable. Host-level rules are
# the only way to route the legacy URLs — and they are *faster* anyway: the
# redirect happens at the edge, before any HTML is served.
#
# Target language is /fr/ because the legacy site was French-only.
# The `.html` suffixes come straight from the brief's old URL list.
# ============================================================================

# Root: `/` is served by the exported language gate (out/index.html), which
# detects the stored/locale preference and forwards to /<locale>/bienvenue/.
# No host rule here, otherwise every visitor would be forced into /fr/.

# ── Legacy URLs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/index.html     /fr/bienvenue/                301
/Repros.html    /fr/produits/cmv-repro        301
/Contact.html   /fr/contact                   301
/Galerie.html   /fr/galerie                   301

# ── Convenience aliases for the URLs people type by hand ────────────────────
/devis          /fr/contact#devis             301
/produits/      /fr/produits/                 200
